From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 18:29:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: pm8941-pwrkey - arm warm reset during probe

The reboot notifier selects the PMIC's PS_HOLD reset type, but a panic
reaches emergency_restart() without calling blocking reboot notifiers.
On a cold-started ThinkSmart View, hardware readback shows reset type 0x08
even though reboot=warm selected REBOOT_WARM. Normal warm reboots preserve
ramoops without ECC errors, whereas a panic after cold startup does not.

When warm reboot is requested, program that reset type during probe as
well. Reuse the existing sleepable configuration path rather than trying
to perform regmap operations from a panic notifier. The reboot notifier
continues to select the requested action for normal reboot and poweroff;
other default reboot modes are unchanged.

Source: local device integration, not an upstream backport.
Base: msm8953-mainline/linux 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429,
with this device's preceding kernel patches applied.
---
 drivers/input/misc/pm8941-pwrkey.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/pm8941-pwrkey.c b/drivers/input/misc/pm8941-pwrkey.c
index 53249d2c0..a065b2789 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/pm8941-pwrkey.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/pm8941-pwrkey.c
@@ -401,6 +401,14 @@ static int pm8941_pwrkey_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 				error);
 			return error;
 		}
+
+		/*
+		 * Panic restart bypasses reboot notifiers. Arm warm reset now
+		 * so emergency restarts can preserve retained crash logs.
+		 */
+		if (reboot_mode == REBOOT_WARM)
+			pm8941_reboot_notify(&pwrkey->reboot_notifier,
+					    SYS_RESTART, NULL);
 	}
 
 	wakeup = pwrkey->data->wakeup_source_default ||
-- 
